          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चोट (coṭ) — \"an injury, a hurt\". It is feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मुझे चोट (coṭ) लगी है — \"I have been hurt\", literally \"a hurt has struck me\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चोट (coṭ) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cuṭati, \"cuts off\" (CDIAL 4857). CDIAL reconstructs a further sense, \"strikes\", and a variant coṭṭ-, and takes the group to be of non-Aryan origin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A way to say you are hurt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
